            <div xml:id="d44">

                <pb facs="0205" n="87" sameAs="frus:frus1928v02/pg87"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.4215 Air Pollution/67: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Canada</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Phillips</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Ottawa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-06-30T13:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 30, 1928—1
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 2:10 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>143. In the absence of Prime Minister this morning presented personally to the
                    Under Secretary of State for External Affairs strong note following your 86 [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">88</hi>], June 29, 8 p.m., regarding Trail smelter. Am
                    making every possible effort to arrange precise terms of reference.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
